  "implemented": [
    "Private row, column, retained-grid split and deferred geometry plans carry cell-prefixed inline atom bindings. The planner uses original table anchors; only execution resolves new cell and paragraph identities.",
    "D01 reconstructs declared paths, offsets, payload identities and source resource descriptors. Removing or altering bindings refuses. Plan-wide birth identity validation includes all cell atom controls and sibling/retained controls.",
    "New cell paragraphs materialize inline math, images, mentions and sources through public native primitives. Source metadata and locks finalize after all topology operations, preventing new controls from blocking a later row insertion in the same plan.",
    "New-cell image resources participate in the existing revision-bound preparation handle. Planning does not fetch or embed; final native image allocation follows staged topology and ordinary content operations.",
    "Six native cases cover rows, columns, simultaneous row/column insertion, retained-grid splits, compound row/split geometry and cell lists. Each has all four atom kinds, complete source targets, single publication, pure D01 decoding, tamper refusal, native Word parts/relationship oracles, history and DOCX reopening.",
    "Native effective cell list markers select HTML table projection. Existing plain/merged GFM behavior stays intact. A blanket auto-table experiment broke an original merged-span acceptance test and was replaced by marker-based selection; the acceptance test is unchanged.",
    "New-cell tracked births refuse before any writer call. Shared native edits require prepared payload storage before publication or history changes.",
    "Eight real shared cases cover row/column atoms, both client orders and reconnect receivers, peer text in retained cells, both histories, media, remote caret geometry and DOCX/room reopening. A ninth case verifies refusal without prepared payload storage."
  ],
  "numberingOracle": "The native core deliberately retains numbering shells and definitions across history, as required by package-shell-history.test.ts. The cell-list undo oracle retains exactly the applied numbering definition and its relationship through an independent native shell seed. All other Word parts and persisted relationships restore exactly. The relationship parser order counter is not an OOXML attribute; all persisted relationship fields remain compared.",
  "remaining": [
    "Undo of row/column birth hides peer text typed into the new cells. The exact failing source and compiled fixtures are retained. This is not claimed passing or resolved by the retained-cell peer tests.",
    "Atoms inside new nested table/registered block cell fragments still require full fragment execution.",
    "Marked/linked image and other unsupported atom ownership paths, and hyperlink reconciliation around retained controls.",
    "Image removal/reference replacement and shared resource retirement.",
    "Tracked inline birth ownership, accept/reject retirement, source scope reconciliation and concurrent same-payload fields.",
    "Installed application SDK cutover and browser feature parity."
  ],
